            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nI don't think this is a good idea for at least these reasons:\n\n- In order to show clues in a 'mini.clue' window, they require a single trigger key. Like `<Leader>`. There is no such universal prefix for 'mini.files' mappings.\n- There is no current or planned functionality for 'mini.clue' window to be open at all times.\n- Help window shows more than buffer mappings, but bookmarks too. It is not possible to show bookmarks in 'mini.clue'.\n- The `g?` to show help is a more or less established convention for Neovim plugins.\n\nIn a way, it can already be partially achieved with a setup like this (which is hardly ergonomic):\n\n```lua\nrequire('mini.files').setup({\n  -- Create mappings with the same `<Leader>` prefix\n  mappings = {\n    close       = '<Leader><Leader>q',\n    go_in       = '<Leader><Leader>l',\n    go_in_plus  = '<Leader><Leader>L',\n    go_out      = '<Leader><Leader>h',\n    go_out_plus = '<Leader><Leader>H',\n    mark_goto   = \"<Leader><Leader>'\",\n    mark_set    = '<Leader><Leader>m',\n    reset       = '<Leader><Leader><BS>',\n    reveal_cwd  = '<Leader><Leader>@',\n    show_help   = '<Leader><Leader>g?',\n    synchronize = '<Leader><Leader>=',\n    trim_left   = '<Leader><Leader><',\n    trim_right  = '<Leader><Leader>>',\n  },\n})\n\n-- Ensure 'mini.clue' is enabled in 'mini.files' buffers\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', {\n  pattern = 'MiniFilesBufferCreate',\n  callback = function(args)\n    require('mini.clue').ensure_buf_triggers(args.data.buf_id)\n  end,\n})\n```\n\nSo I think this is a safe to close as \"not planned\".",
            "created_at": "2026-04-24T16:15:08Z",
